:m **Sequential memory access patterns:**
```c
// Good - sequential
for (i = 0; i < n; i++)
for (j = 0; j < n; j++)
sum += A[i][j];
// Row-major, sequential
// Bad - strided
for (j = 0; j < n; j++)
for (i = 0; i < n; i++)
sum += A[i][j];
// Column access, cache misses
```
5-10x performance difference!

:m **Divide work into blocks** that fit in cache:
```c
// Block size = L1 cache size / element size
block_size = 64;
for (ii = 0; ii < n; ii += block_size)
for (jj = 0; jj < n; jj += block_size)
// Process block - stays in cache
```
Blocks reused multiple times before eviction.

